    "chunks": [
      "Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Musa (may God be pleased with him) narrated to us. He said: Muhammad ibn Abi Abdillah al-Kufi narrated to us. He said: Musa ibn Imran al-Nakhai narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn al-Hakam, from Amr ibn Jubayr, from his father, from Abu Ja'far al-Baqir (peace be upon him). He said:",
      "The Messenger of Allah sent Ali to Yemen. A horse escaped and kicked a man, killing him. The relatives brought him before Ali, who ruled the owner not liable. The relatives came to the Prophet complaining. The Prophet said: Ali is not an oppressor and was not created for oppression. The guardianship after me belongs to Ali; his judgment is his judgment and his word is his word. No one rejects them except a disbeliever, and no one accepts them except a believer. The Yemenis accepted. The Prophet said: This is your repentance."
    ],
